{"parentUuid":"b0f95a8a-c430-4b08-8fb4-c747b4a602fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DmjHxWAgoqtqjiGp3Rsqf6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014aijRhodfYc5UpK8TvnHTG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\project_prime_silo_offload_orchestrator.md","content":"---\nname: project_prime_silo_offload_orchestrator\ndescription: ADR-004 local offload orchestrator — route execution to Benny, reserve Claude for planning; manifest+gate+digest design, Phases 0-4 implemented on branch feat/local-offload-orchestrator\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nBuilt to cut Claude credit/token burn on prime-silo dev: offload the bulk of *execution* to the local model (Benny), keep Claude for planning/strategy/adjudication. Operator hypothesis: ≥75% of tasks offloadable.\n\n**Key insight (drove the whole design):** offloading execution alone saves nothing — the cost is tokens *through Claude's context*. Savings come from (1) Claude writes a compact manifest, (2) an eval gate absorbs verbose output locally, (3) Claude reads back only a digest, escalated to only on fail/ambiguity.\n\n**Design = local-first executor with an audit gate, two lanes one gate:**\n- Contract: `aamp.offload_task/1` (`manifests/offload/task.manifest.schema.json`) — intent + testable acceptance_criteria + risk_tier.\n- Router (`router.matrix.json` + `runtime/benny/core/offload/router.py`): green/yellow/red; may UPGRADE never downgrade; guarded paths (L1/L2/manifests/, signing) + security intents force red.\n- Gate (`gate.py`): deterministic checks first (all exit 0), then LLM judge for yellow only. Anti-collusion: judge model ≠ executor model, flags+low-confidence if equal; deterministic checks are the hard backstop.\n- Executor (`executor.py`): shell or generate (via existing `resolve_executor` in local_executor.py). Output is a PROPOSED artifact → outbox, never a direct write to deterministic zone (respects ADR-001 HITL promotion).\n- Orchestrator (`orchestrator.py`): submit→route→execute→gate→digest; full artifact to `$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/<ws>/offload/outbox/`, only compact digest back to planner.\n- Ledger (`ledger.py`) + `scripts/offload-report.mjs`: honest components, offload_rate is the headline, 75% is a target to MEASURE not assert (memo-ray token-audit lesson).\n\n**Routing rule:** if you can write crisp testable acceptance_criteria up front → offloadable; if \"done\" needs judgment → Claude keeps it (red).\n\n**Surfaces:** FastAPI `runtime/benny/api/offload_routes.py` mounted `/api/offload` (submit?wait=, validate, result, queue, ledger); MCP `offload_exec` tool in `mcp/server.js` (sync lane, returns digest only); `scripts/offload-runner.mjs` (async inbox drain, --watch); `scripts/offload-report.mjs`.\n\n**Status:** branch `feat/local-offload-orchestrator`. 17/17 network-free tests pass (`runtime/tests/core/test_offload.py`). UNVERIFIED: generate + LLM-judge paths against a real local model (Lemonade/Ollama/FLM) and the actual offload rate — needs a running local server; ledger is the instrument. Full design in `runtime/architecture/ADR-004-local-offload-orchestrator.md`. Not yet committed/PR'd at write time.\n\nRelates to [[project_open_studio_opencode_audit]] (4-seam audit pattern reused as the gate), [[memo_ray_token_audit_validation]] (honesty discipline), [[project_prime_silo_vision_ingestion]] (vision fidelity judge = judge pattern precedent).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":229,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2496,"cache_read_input_tokens":129862,"output_tokens":1427,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2496,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":229,"output_