ided` is exactly this gap, measured.\n\n## Where the real leverage is\n\n| Step | Who pays | On your meter? |\n|------|----------|----------------|\n| Write 15-line manifest | me | yes, but tiny |\n| Read the file | Benny | **no** |\n| Generate the code | Benny | **no** |\n| Run lint/tests (gate) | Benny | **no** |\n| Read back the digest | me | yes, ~40 tokens |\n| Promote/sign the result | you | n/a |\n\n## The honest catch\n\nIt only saves tokens **when the task stays green/yellow and passes.** If it fails or escalates, I get pulled back in and read the artifact after all — so you pay for the round trip *plus* my involvement. That's why the routing rule matters: I should only offload when I can write crisp `acceptance_criteria` up front. Architecture, ambiguous specs, security — those are 🔴 red, I keep them, and offloading them would *cost* you, not save.\n\nSo in practice the win is: **you spend my tokens on deciding what to do and judging whether it's right; Benny spends free local compute on the typing.** The `offload-report.mjs` ledger tells you whether that's actually happening (offload rate) rather than us assuming it.\n\n## Two honest gaps before this saves you anything real\n\n1. **It's not wired into *this* Claude Code session.** The `offload_exec` tool lives in prime-silo's own MCP server (`mcp/server.js`) — for *me* to call it here, that server has to be registered as an MCP server in your Claude Code config. Right now I can't actually invoke it; I can only describe it. Want me to add it to your MCP config so it's a live tool next session?\n2. **The local model path is unverified** — needs Benny's runtime up with a model loaded. Until then the digests come back as \"executor unavailable → escalated,\" which saves nothing.\n\nWant me to do #1 (register the MCP server) so the loop is actually usable?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":126,"cache_read_input_tokens":1