{"parentUuid":"93b5df9a-5b6e-45c6-91f9-20c0459a353e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01BPSgEeZ1wEMNpDmmrtoCrF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done — `Phi-4-mini-instruct-NPU` is the default judge now, and the whole judge investigation is recorded honestly. Committed (`ec4c7e4`).\n\n## The answer on Phi-4-mini\n\nIt's the **right choice, for a specific reason** — not because it's a good judge, but because its *failure mode is safe*:\n\n- It reliably **rejects bad code** (0.0, consistent, ~5s, clean JSON — the things R1 and the 0.5B couldn't do).\n- It **false-negatives good code** (escalates work that was actually fine).\n- The 0.5B did the opposite and **rubber-stamped broken code at 0.9** — a false positive, which for a gate is the dangerous direction (it ships a defect).\n\nFor a gate, **never-pass-bad-work > never-escalate-good-work**, so Phi wins. I made it the default, kept the `run_judge` hardening (forced JSON + retry), and wrote [JUDGE-CALIBRATION.md](prime-silo/manifests/offload/JUDGE-CALIBRATION.md) with the measured grid so nobody has to re-derive this.\n\n## The honest bigger picture this surfaced\n\nThe judge-model rabbit hole (R1 → 9b → Phi → 0.5B) taught us something more important than which model to pick: **none of the small local judges are reliable enough to *pass* work.** Four mitigations didn't fix the miscalibration — they're just weak judges.\n\nSo the realistic token-savings map is:\n\n| Task type | Savings today |\n|---|---|\n| 🟢 **GREEN** — `shell`/deterministic codemods, formatting, scaffolds with `verify` | **Reliable** — the deterministic gate proves correctness, no LLM judgment needed |\n| 🟡 **YELLOW** — judged `generate` tasks | **Modest** — Phi escalates a lot of good work, so they bounce back to me |\n| 🔴 **RED** | None (by design — I keep them) |\n\nThat's not a flaw in the architecture — the deterministic gate is the trustworthy tier and it's doing its job; the LLM judge sits on top as advisory and escalates when unsure. It *is* an honest ceiling on the 75% target: **the green deterministic lane is where the savings live until a stronger non-reasoning judge model loads on your box.**\n\nThe single highest-leverage thing you could do to raise the yellow-task ceiling is get a capable instruct model serving — which loops back to the **GGUF `llama-server` load failures** (Gemma etc. won't start). Want me to dig into that next, or pause here? Everything's committed on `feat/local-offload-orchestrator` (7 commits, still local)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":978,"cache_read_input_tokens":234716,"output_tokens":1009,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":978,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1009,"cache_read_input_tokens":234716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":978},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcYFPLYp4oQbwKG7QePYU","type":"assistant","uuid":"b1f93b07-2153-4880-ae50-f8d4b55a2bb4","timestamp":"2026-06-29T21:19:22.577Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"8167e2d7-875f-405a-8e42-ec6b38305c5f","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
