lk of *execution* to the local model (Benny), keep Claude for planning/strategy/adjudication. Operator hypothesis: ≥75% of tasks offloadable.\n\n**Key insight (drove the whole design):** offloading execution alone saves nothing — the cost is tokens *through Claude's context*. Savings come from (1) Claude writes a compact manifest, (2) an eval gate absorbs verbose output locally, (3) Claude reads back only a digest, escalated to only on fail/ambiguity.\n\n**Design = local-first executor with an audit gate, two lanes one gate:**\n- Contract: `aamp.offload_task/1` (`manifests/offload/task.manifest.schema.json`) — intent + testable acceptance_criteria + risk_tier.\n- Router (`router.matrix.json` + `runtime/benny/core/offload/router.py`): green/yellow/red; may UPGRADE never downgrade; guarded paths (L1/L2/manifests/, signing) + security intents force red.\n- Gate (`gate.py`): deterministic checks first (all exit 0), then LLM judge for yellow only. Anti-collusion: judge model ≠ executor model, flags+low-confidence if equal; deterministic checks are the hard backstop.\n- Executor (`executor.py`): shell or generate (via existing `resolve_executor` in local_executor.py). Output is a PROPOSED artifact → outbox, never a direct write to deterministic zone (respects ADR-001 HITL promotion).\n- Orchestrator (`orchestrator.py`): submit→route→execute→gate→digest; full artifact to `$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/<ws>/offload/outbox/`, only compact digest back to planner.\n- Ledger (`ledger.py`) + `scripts/offload-report.mjs`: honest components, offload_rate is the headline, 75% is a target to MEASURE not assert (memo-ray token-audit lesson).\n\n**Routing rule:** if you can write crisp testable acceptance_criteria up front → offloadable; if \"done\" needs judgment → Claude keeps it (red).\n\n**shell-vs-generate invariant (honesty fix):** a `generate` task is an UNAPPLIED proposal in the outbox (ADR-001) — deterministic checks run against the live repo and validate STALE code, not the artifact → false pass. So router upgrades EVERY generate task green→yellow and gate refuses to auto-pass a generate proposal without a judge (judge reads artifact text = only valid evaluator). `shell` tasks act in place → gate validates real effect → stay true-green. Green example is now a shell codemod (green-format-imports), not generate.\n\n**Surfaces:** FastAPI `runtime/benny/api/offload_routes.py` mounted `/api/offload` (submit?wait=, validate, result, queue, ledger); MCP `offload_exec` tool in `mcp/server.js` (sync lane, returns digest only); `scripts/offload-runner.mjs` (async inbox drain, --watch); `scripts/offload-report.mjs`.\n\n**Status:** branch `feat/local-offload-orchestrator`. 17/17 network-free tests pass (`runtime/tests/core/test_offload.py`). VERIFIED LIVE (2026-06-29) against Lemonade: generate+judge end-to-end. DEFAULT EXECUTOR = `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (clean correct code, judge 0.95, no reasoning-dump); judge = `lemonade/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-CPU` (distinct→collusion False). digest ~512 chars while artifact stayed in outbox. qwen3-tk-4b-FLM also passes (0.85) but buries code in chain-of-thought. honest escalation confirmed when executor model 500'd. JUDGE MODEL findings (measured, manifests/offload/JUDGE-CALIBRATION.md): DEFAULT JUDGE = `lemonade/Phi-4-mini-instruct-NPU`. Small local judges are NOT reliable enough to PASS work — 0.5B false-POSITIVED broken code (0.9, dangerous); Phi-4-mini false-NEGATIVES good code (safe — rejects bad, escalates good); deepseek-r1-8b-FLM unusable (reasons in prose, 68s, never emits JSON even with enable_thinking:false which FLM ignores). Chose Phi because never-pass-bad > never-escalate-good for a gate. CONSEQUENCE: yellow (judged generate) tasks often escalate even when good → few token savings there; RELIABLE SAVINGS COME FROM GREEN shell/deterministic tasks + verify-able criteria. run_judge hardened: response_format json_object + 1 retry + think-strip + last-balanced-JSON parse (forced-JSON + retry did NOT fix the None/miscalibration — the models are just weak). Gating dependency for better yellow savings: a more capable non-reasoning instruct model that loads (Gemma GGUF won't). GGUF/llamacpp (Gemma-*) + Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-NPU recipes FAIL to load llama-server on the operator's box — working models are FLM + ONNX-CPU; matrix defaults re-pointed accordingly. STILL UNVERIFIED: actual offload RATE on a real task stream (ledger is the instrument; needs volume). MCP registered: added `binary16/.mcp.json` (prime-silo .mcp.json uses relative path, only loads when launched from prime-silo/); offload_exec needs Claude Code restart + project-server approval, AND the Benny FastAPI at :8005 restarted to load offload_routes (old process returns 404). Full design in `runtime/architecture/ADR-004-local-offload-orchestrator.md`.\n\nRelates to [[project_open_studio_opencode_audit]] (4-seam audit pattern reused as the gate), [[memo_ray_token_audit_validation]] (honesty discipline), [[project_prime_silo_vision_ingestion]] (vision fidelity judge = judge pattern precedent).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":6,"newStart":25,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," **Surfaces:** FastAPI `runtime/benny/api/offload_routes.py` mounted `/api/offload` (submit?wait=, validate, result, queue, ledger); MCP `offload_exec` tool in `mcp/server.js` (sync lane, returns digest only); `scripts/offload-runner.mjs` (async inbox drain, --watch); `scripts/offload-report.mjs`."," ","-**Status:** branch `feat/local-offload-orchestrator`. 17/17 network-free tests pass (`runtime/tests/core/test_offload.py`). VERIFIED LIVE (2026-06-29) against Lemonade: generate+judge end-to-end. DEFAULT EXECUTOR = `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (clean correct code, judge 0.95, no reasoning-dump); judge = `lemonade/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-CPU` (distinct→collusion False). digest ~512 chars while artifact stayed in outbox. qwen3-tk-4b-FLM also passes (0.85) but buries code in chain-of-thought. honest escalation confirmed when executor model 500'